a few years ago in order to get  respectable power from a gaming laptop  it needed to be big and bulky and even  the largest gaming laptops couldn't come  close to competing with their desktop  counterparts  well now that gaming laptops are using  desktop class GPUs that's all beginning  to change origin PCs Evo 15s for  instance represents a powerful but  portable solution does it make  compromises in the name of portability  well yes but there's still a lot to like  about it let's get into it for a gaming  laptop the Evo 15s is very thin at 0.7  inches it's also relatively light  weighing just four pounds the laptop  uses a 15.6 inch IPS display which  offers vivid accurate colors and wide  viewing in the native 1080p resolution  is great for a gaming laptop this side  laptop features a mostly gloss finish  which looks nice but can attracting  offense the keyboard uses  run-of-the-mill chiclet style keys which  feel competent to type and game on it  also offers RGB backlighting across  three colors own a trackpad responds  pretty well though we would have  preferred a dedicated left and right  click buttons to prevent accidental  clicks the chassis is mostly made of  plastic which results in some minor  undesirable flexing when we gamed on the  notebook the typing surface never got  hot but it did get moderately loud  portable gaming notebooks usually don't  offer a lot of ports but the evil 15s  delightfully surprises here the laptop  offers a plethora of connections that  include three USB 3.0 ports a mini  display fourth HDMI port and more it has  enough ports for either the oculus rift  or HTC vive which makes it a great  portable VR system on the go perhaps our  biggest gripe with the design is the  placement of the power button which is  situated to the front right of the  chassis you may inadvertently turn off  the computer if you're not being careful  the brains behind the laptop is Intel's  quad core i7 7700 HQ CPU which can turbo  up to 3.8 gigahertz the mobile processor  is paired with 16 gigabytes of ddr4 Ram  clocked at 2400 megahertz  Nvidia's GeForce GTX 1060 drives the  graphics here  it's a great GPU that pairs well with  the panel's 1080p resolution for storage  the Evo 15s uses Samsung's high-end SM  961 nvme SSD you can get it and either  256 or 512 gigabytes guarantee our unit  features the latter it's also  supplemented by a happy 2 terabyte 5400  rpm hard drive overall the system specs  are well balanced and represent a  moderately high-end rig we're going to  benchmark the Evo 15 s alongside HD to a  17-inch Omen gaming laptop which is  equipped with a gtx 1070 i7 6700 HQ and  16 gigabytes of RAM while The Omen uses  a slightly older skylake CPU because it  is significantly bigger and equipped  with a higher tier GPU you shouldn't  expect the same level of performance  it's here to give you a point of  comparison for our benchmarks we ran all  games at the respective max settings at  1080p to really stress test the system  our performance data shows that the evil  15s should be able to max out most games  at 1080p with playable framerates  running the lives of the Tomb Raider  benchmark with graphics settings maxed  out origin pcs laptop was able to run  over 60 average fps and more graphically  demanding games like the division and  Metro last light it did dip into the 40s  and 50s but was still highly playable  the laptop couldn't max out Deus Ex  mankind divided though which is one of  the most graphically demanding games on  the market we tried to max out i toast  montreal stealth action game the evil  15s barely made it over 10 FPS the  laptop was able to run the benchmark at  57 average FPS when we disabled  anti-aliasing and lowered the game to  its high preset though when we ran valve  steamvr benchmark the origin PC laptops  produced nine thousand four hundred  eighty seven frames which not only makes  it v already but puts it in the high  tier while the Allman's faster GPU  allows it to pull ahead in games the evo  15s a speedier nvme SSD allows it to  beat HP's notebook in sequential read  and write tests by 115 and 442 percent  respectively  this means Origen laptop really kills it  whenever you need to transfer large  files according to our Cinebench CPU  test evil 15s is 16 percent faster than  single threaded applications and  percent faster in multicolored workloads  these tests indicate that origin PCs  laptop make it a stronger productivity  workhorse in the HP omen for battery  tests we looped the graphically  demanding Unigine value benchmark until  the laptop keeled over this represents a  worst-case gaming scenario here  origins laptop lasted roughly an hour  which isn't great you're most likely  want to bring the charger with you if  you intend to game on the go while you  can find gaming laptops that are more  powerful there's a lot to like about the  evil 15s for a gaming notebook it's thin  light offers a surprising amount of  ports in terms of specs it offers a ton  of those and whistles and should be able  to max that most games at 1080p its  biggest hurdle is its $2,300 price tip  you're really paying for the portable  form factor here it's size and weight  aren't big priorities for you you're  looking for something to lug around to  land parties something like the omen  might be more up your alley HP 17 inch  gaming laptop might be nearly twice as  heavy but you can get it with a more  powerful GTX 1074 around $1,800 if you  have the money and want good specs and a  sleek form factor though origin pcs Evo  15s should definitely be on your radar  for the full written review head on over  to GameSpot calm and if you liked this  video give it a thumbs up and subscribe  to us on youtube thank you for watching  you
 

